---
epr-meta-version: 1
id: rust-style-gate
covers: subtree
purpose: >
  The native Rust style checker shared by agent advice and reach gates. Syntax detection,
  Git-derived debt baselines and strict scope resolution live here; runtime adapters do
  not implement another lint evaluator.
rules:
  - id: rust-style-strict
    policy: rust-style-strict@1
---
# Rust style gate

This tool is its own first permanently strict scope. RS-GOV-04 requires a reason on every
lint suppression, including tests, inactive cfg branches and literal macro-generated attributes.
The native eprfs-meta resolver owns scope inheritance. Git owns the debt baseline; there is no
editable debt allowance to widen. Plain `allow` and `expect` without reasons cannot be excepted.
